Land Grab (N64brew Game Jam 2024, code/landgrab at 0dea720) for the Fire TV remote.

A remote has OK, a direction ring, MENU, PLAY/PAUSE, rewind and fast-forward, and n64rt makes each
of the last four tap-or-hold (N64_REMOTE_MAP_DEFAULT in apps/n64-landgrab/CMakeLists.txt):
OK = A (place), MENU = Start (pause), hold MENU = B (skip turn), PLAY/PAUSE = R (flip),
hold PLAY/PAUSE = L (mirror), << / >> = C-left / C-right (change piece),
hold << / >> = C-down / C-up (smaller / bigger piece).

This patch makes the game say so:
  - the random hints name the remote's buttons instead of B, L/Z, R and the C buttons;
  - the control legend (scoreboard_controls_render) draws remote buttons, our own icons from
    n64/jam24/assets-remote/landgrab (make-icons.py), instead of the joypad icons;
  - "Hold" is written in gold (a new squarewave font style, FONT_STYLE_GOLD / FMT_HOLD);
  - the pause screen quits on a held B (half a second; holding MENU sends B), which a remote can
    do, as well as on A + B + Start, which it can't.

n64/jam24/Makefile applies it to a copy of code/landgrab in the build directory, so the jam
checkout stays as fetched. The build stops if it no longer applies.

